id: karmic-chance
name: Karmic Chance
kind: karma
cost: 1
description: >
  You manage to override random chance through sheer force of will.
text: >
  After seeing the result of any die, you may use this Karmic Effect to
  reroll that die. You must accept this second roll, unless it is lower than
  the first. In which case, you may take the first roll.

---

# reroll() replaces the Base Die outright and reads the result again from
# scratch - so a new Critical rolls its dice, a new Botch takes its 2(bT), and
# whichever the first die scored is gone rather than carried over.
# When the second roll comes out lower you are asked whether to keep the first,
# which is the one part of it that is your choice rather than arithmetic.
# No `requires`, and that is deliberate: the rule is "any die", so this is
# offered on a lone Skill roll or Steadfast Check as well as on a Clash, and it
# does not ask whether you passed. Rerolling a roll that already succeeded is
# strange, but it is what the effect says you may do.
# Not automated: rerolling a die other than the Base Die - a Wound Roll's own
# dice, say. The system can only reach the one that decided the result.

[triggered/clash-resolved]
reroll();
